## Hints for Future Agents
The post-commit hook automatically pushes master and can rebase. Disable hooks per invocation for a local commit unless publication is explicitly authorized. Do not restore the automatic dashboard invocation. Standards and requirements are gathered once by the orchestrating agent into context/standards.md and context/spec.md; build_prompt.sh embeds them for each reviewer. Missing requirements must be reported as Spec not assessed. Keep design judgments subordinate to repository conventions. A single reviewer's demonstrated serious defect outranks a minor consensus concern. The CLI/model defaults and reviewer runner were not changed. The skill validator needs PyYAML, which is available through uv's temporary environment.

## Codebase Discoveries
The old panel helper always chose the repository default branch, while the standalone dashboard already resolved actual PR targets. The panel helper now validates PR branch/head identity, recovers PRs through the wtpr breadcrumb or branch search, uses the actual PR base, and pins BASE_SHA, MERGE_BASE, and HEAD_SHA. A PR whose target is unavailable fails rather than silently reviewing the default branch. A branch with commits but an empty final diff is rejected. Existing prompt fencing also handles the newly embedded standards and spec context. Skill installation uses symlinks, so edits are active after make install-skills. All five changed files are human-authored; no generated files were committed.

